      <!-- RESEARCH BEHIND THE DESIGN -->
      <h2>What I tested before recommending it</h2>
      <p>
        A parsed page can look convincing while the assistant still retrieves incomplete evidence. I therefore checked
        the end of the path as well as the beginning. The important question was whether a user’s query brought back
        the rule together with the note that changed how it should be applied. Keeping the document fixed made that
        check repeatable after every repair. I also tried multi-page OCR, image-based retrieval, and three ways of
        representing flowcharts to see where each approach helped and where it quietly dropped a relationship.
      </p>
