        },
        {
          title: 'Embedding pages as images',
          body: 'A page image keeps its layout, so image-based retrieval seemed promising. The boundary between pages still remained. Embedding one page at a time separated a later note from the sentence that cited it. In the RAGFlow path I evaluated, a vision model first described the image and the system searched that description. Reconstructing the relationship explicitly gave me more control over which pieces of evidence retrieval could return together.'
        },
        {
